# mail2 env — copy to `.env` for local overrides. None of these are required:
# the app boots without this file. The dev script loads `.env` itself
# (`node --env-file-if-exists=.env`, because SvelteKit does not put `.env`
# values into process.env), so restart the dev server after changing it.
# Real environment variables win over `.env` values.

# Session sharing with webmail 1.0. The session cookie holds an id that each
# app looks up in ONE SQLite store; by default that store is per-app
# (`<cwd>/.data/store.sqlite`), so mail2 cannot see sessions created by
# webmail. Point at webmail's store — relative to this app's directory:
STORE_DB_PATH=../webmail/.data/store.sqlite

# Only for tunnel/hostname testing (README → "Testing over the network"): the
# parent-domain cookie that makes the login from webmail-dev.zaur.app visible
# on mail2-dev.zaur.app. While set, plain localhost logins BREAK (browsers
# reject a .zaur.app cookie coming from localhost), so keep it commented
# except during a tunnel test — prefer passing it inline on the command line:
# SESSION_COOKIE_DOMAIN=.zaur.app

# Required only when NODE_ENV=production. Session records in the store are
# sealed with it — two apps sharing one store must share the same value.
# SESSION_SECRET=

# Optional: JMAP server used for proxied requests. Defaults to the server URL
# stored in the session account (the live mail.zaur.app in dev).
# JMAP_INTERNAL_URL=
